.TH WLIST-ADD 1 "17 November 2026" "version 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
wlist-add \- Add item to registry.
.SH SYNOPSIS
wlist add [path/to/database] 
--name <item> | -n <item> [--quantity <amount> | -a <amount>]
[--priority <priority level> | -p <priority level>]
[--url <url> | -u <url>]
[--notes <Notes>...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add an item to the registry.
.PP
The add subcommand can be used to add an item 
to the registry with all the data that you know.
.PP
The only required information is the name of the item.
.PP
If no path to database is given,
the program will try to open a database located in
.B wishlist
in your home directory named
.B gift_registry.db.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -n <item>, --name <item>
The item desired.
.TP
.B -q <amount>, --quantity <amount>
The quantity of the specified item.
.PP
If no quantity is specified, 
it will be assumed to be 1.
.TP
.B -p <priority level>, --priority <priority level>
How much you want the item.
.PP
The value can be one of the following:
.RS
.IP
low
.IP
medium
.IP
high
.IP
highest
.RE
.PP
If no value is given, low is assumed.
.TP
.B -u <url>, --url <url>
The URL for the item.
.PP
If this is not specified, the URL will be **/**.
.TP
.B --notes <Notes>...
A list of notes regarding the item.
.PP
When providing a note, 
make sure to put the note in quotes,
unless the note is only one word.
.PP
If quotes are not used, 
each item is considered its own note.
.PP
If not provided, this will simply be left empty.
.SH AUTHOR
Bryce Campbell (tonyhawk2100@gmail.com)
.SH EXAMPLES
Add item to registry:
.RS
.IP
wlist add -n "Mario Kart" 
.RE
.PP
Add item with a note:
.RS
.IP
wlist add -name "Mario Kart" --notes "Only if I get Switch 2."
.RE
.PP
Add item with two notes:
.RS
.IP
wlist -name "Mario Kart --notes "Only if I get Switch 2." "Physical only."
.RE
.PP
Add item with priority level:
.RS
.IP
wlist add -n "Mario Kart" -p high
.RE
.PP
Add item with URL:
.RS
.IP
wlist add -name "Mario Kart" -u https://example.com/mario-kart
.RE
.PP
Add item a quantity of more than 1:
.RS
wlist add -n "Mario Kart" -q 2
.RE